  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anticipating and Responding to El Ni&#xf1;o, a multi-sectoral Early Warning and Livelihood Response Project (REACT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this $1.375m FAO project is to provide life-saving cash, livelihood and early warning support to flood risk households. The project will provide unconditional cash transfers to 3,675 households (22,050 individuals) for three months, while also supporting animal health and vector control measures to prevent diseases associated with contaminated floodwaters. In total, the project targets 60,450 people, including 16,019 women and 13,601 girls, and including approximately 9,068 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
